message.content:
The bug was caused by using `.items()` on `received_params` (which is a `MultiDict` in the case of `QueryParams` or `Headers`) when extracting extra parameters for a Pydantic model with `extra="allow"`. In a `MultiDict`, `.items()` only returns the last value for each key, causing multiple values for the same parameter to be truncated.

I fixed this by checking if `received_params` is an instance of `ImmutableMultiDict` or `Headers`. If so, I use `.keys()` and `.getlist(key)` to retrieve all values for each extra parameter. If there is only one value, it is passed as a scalar; otherwise, it is passed as a list, matching the behavior of `_extract_form_body`.

Verified the fix with a reproduction script that tests both single and multiple values for extra parameters.

